import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.DaD4z1Q-.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Load prefixed packages with the autoloader","description":"How Strauss-RS writes autoload.php and a classmap, how to load them early or through Composer, and how to delete the original vendor packages.","frontmatter":{"title":"Load prefixed packages with the autoloader","description":"How Strauss-RS writes autoload.php and a classmap, how to load them early or through Composer, and how to delete the original vendor packages."},"headers":[],"relativePath":"guide/autoloader.md","filePath":"guide/autoloader.md"}`),a={name:`guide/autoloader.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="the-autoloader" tabindex="-1">The autoloader <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-autoloader" aria-label="Permalink to “The autoloader”">​</a></h1><p><code>prefix</code> writes two files into the target directory: <code>autoload.php</code> and <code>autoload-classmap.php</code>. Your plugin has to load <code>autoload.php</code> before it uses any prefixed class.</p><h2 id="loading-it" tabindex="-1">Loading it <a class="header-anchor" href="#loading-it" aria-label="Permalink to “Loading it”">​</a></h2><p>The simplest way is <code>include_autoloader</code>:</p><div class="language-json"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">json</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark" style="--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">{</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">	&quot;include_autoloader&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">: </span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">true</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">}</span></span></code></pre></div><p>After prefixing, this adds a line to <code>vendor/autoload.php</code> that loads the prefixed packages. Composer rewrites <code>vendor/autoload.php</code> whenever it installs or updates, so run <code>prefix</code> after those. The Composer scripts in <a href="./getting-started.html#_3-run-it-from-composer">getting started</a> do that. You can also run it once with <code>sh bin/strauss-rs.sh include-autoloader</code>. It is safe to run again.</p><p>If you would rather load it yourself, require the file from your plugin:</p><div class="language-php"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">php</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark" style="--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">require_once</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> __DIR__</span><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> .</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> &#39;/vendor-prefixed/autoload.php&#39;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">;</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id="code-execution-order" tabindex="-1">Code execution order <a class="header-anchor" href="#code-execution-order" aria-label="Permalink to “Code execution order”">​</a></h2><p>Remember that your prefixed classes and symbols don&#39;t become available until the <code>vendor-prefixed</code> <code>autoload.php</code> file is included.</p><p>For early-execution scripts, such as an <code>object-cache.php</code> drop-in, an <code>advanced-cache.php</code> drop-in, or a firewall that boots from <code>wp-config.php</code> in Wordpress, you will need to ensure that the autoloader is included before attempting to use any prefixed classes or symbols.</p><h2 id="classmap-or-fallback" tabindex="-1">Classmap or fallback <a class="header-anchor" href="#classmap-or-fallback" aria-label="Permalink to “Classmap or fallback”">​</a></h2><p>By default (<code>optimize_autoloader: true</code>) the autoloader is classmap-authoritative. Every class is listed under its new name, so loading a class never searches the disk.</p><p>Set <code>&quot;optimize_autoloader&quot;: false</code> to also fall back to each package&#39;s PSR-4 folders, using the renamed namespaces, for classes that are not in the classmap, such as files added after <code>prefix</code> ran. Packages that use <code>psr-0</code> are only loaded through the classmap, and you get a warning if there are any.</p><h2 id="files-that-always-load" tabindex="-1">Files that always load <a class="header-anchor" href="#files-that-always-load" aria-label="Permalink to “Files that always load”">​</a></h2><p>Packages can list <code>files</code> in their autoload section, usually for helper functions. The generated <code>autoload.php</code> requires those files for you.</p><h2 id="turning-the-autoloader-off" tabindex="-1">Turning the autoloader off <a class="header-anchor" href="#turning-the-autoloader-off" aria-label="Permalink to “Turning the autoloader off”">​</a></h2><p><code>classmap_output</code> controls whether the two files are written at all. If you leave it out, it is <code>false</code> when the target directory is already part of your project&#39;s own <code>autoload</code> (Composer is loading it), and <code>true</code> otherwise.</p><h2 id="deleting-the-originals" tabindex="-1">Deleting the originals <a class="header-anchor" href="#deleting-the-originals" aria-label="Permalink to “Deleting the originals”">​</a></h2><p>Once the packages have been copied and prefixed, the originals in <code>vendor/</code> are extra weight in a release. Set <code>delete_vendor_packages</code> to remove them:</p><div class="language-json"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">json</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark" style="--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">{</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">	&quot;delete_vendor_packages&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">: </span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">true</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">}</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Composer&#39;s own autoloader still lists those packages and would stop on their missing <code>files</code>, so after deleting, <code>prefix</code>:</p><ol><li>removes the deleted packages from <code>vendor/composer/installed.json</code>, and</li><li>runs <code>composer dump-autoload --no-scripts</code> to rebuild Composer&#39;s autoloader from what is left.</li></ol><p>If <code>composer</code> is not on your <code>PATH</code>, set <code>STRAUSS_RS_COMPOSER</code> to the command to run. If it cannot be run, <code>prefix</code> warns and tells you what to do by hand. Nothing is deleted in a <code>--dry-run</code>.</p><p>Because the packages are gone from <code>installed.json</code>, the next <code>prefix</code> needs them back, so run <code>composer install</code> first. Hooking <code>prefix</code> onto <code>post-install-cmd</code> and <code>post-update-cmd</code> does this for you.</p>`,25)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};